nfigured, list immediate remediation steps, and provide redacted strings you can paste into the ticket.\n\nWhat’s misconfigured / insecure\n- DEBUG=true in staging — debug mode should be off in any environment accessible outside a developer machine; it can leak stack traces, source, and secrets.\n- ALLOWED_HOSTS=* — allows host header attacks and should be limited to explicit hostnames/IPs for staging.\n- Secrets in a shared doc (DB password + admin token) — docs and chat systems are commonly indexed/backed up; these credentials are exposed and must be rotated.\n- Admin token in URL query param — tokens in URLs can leak via logs, referrers, and browser history. Use Authorization headers or short‑lived session cookies instead.\n- DB credentials in plaintext connection string — should be stored in a secrets manager, not in visible configs/docs.\n- Potential excessive DB user privileges — svc_admin name suggests an elevated account; ensure least privilege for the app user.\n- No explicit TLS/sslmode for DB connection — ensure DB connections require TLS (sslmode=require or equivalent).\n\nImmediate actions (in order)\n1. Remove the leaked config from the shared doc and any other place it was copied to.\n2. Rotate the exposed secrets immediately:\n   - Change the DB user's password.\n   - Revoke/replace the admin token.\n3. Revoke any sessions that used the leaked token; issue a new token with short TTL and rotate credentials used by services.\n4. Set DEBUG=false in staging.\n5. Replace ALLOWED_HOSTS=* with the exact hostnames used by staging (e.g., admin-stg.internal, api-stg.internal).\n6. Ensure DB connections require TLS (e.g., add sslmode=require) and store DB credentials in a secrets manager (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, etc.).\n7. Audit access logs for both the admin app and DB for suspicious activity, and record who viewed the shared doc.\n8. Implement secret scanning on repositories/docs and restrict sharing permissions on docs.\n9. Review svc_admin privileges and create a less-privileged app user if appropriate.\n\nRedacted strings for the ticket (safe to include)\n- Database connection (redacted): postgres://svc_admin:<REDACTED_DB_PASSWORD>@db-stg.internal:5432/core\n- Admin URL (redacted): https://admin-stg.internal/ops?token=<REDACTED_ADMIN_TOKEN>\n\nSuggested ticket text to paste\n- \"Staging config leaked to shared doc. Please rotate DB password for svc_admin and revoke the exposed admin token immediately. Remove secrets from the doc and replace with secrets-manager references. Also set DEBUG=false and restrict ALLOWED_HOSTS to staging hostnames. Audit access logs for the period [insert times].\"\n- Attach the redacted strings above for reference.\n\nIf you want, I can draft a short incident notification to send to the team or a checklist for rotating the credentials and validating deployments.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0752de9ee50b6647016a9a087a49ec87d0a08ff11456ce8bd3","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"in_memory","reasoning":{"context":"current_turn","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","status":"completed","store":false,"temperature":1.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":1.0,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":335,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1681,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1024},"total_tokens":2016},"user":null},"durationMs":15558.893291978166,"headers":{"access-control-expose-headers":"X-Request-ID, CF-Ray, C